Derived from that project:

  hooks/always-on.mjs
      Direct port. Two deliberate changes: the opt-in flag check is removed
      (the standard is unconditional here), and failure is loud instead of
      silent. The file carries an attribution header.

  standard/INTERACTION-STANDARD.md
      Rules F1, F5 (step economy), F7, F9, F10, F11 and F12 are adopted or
      adapted from that project's rules R10, R2, R9, R5, R6, R8 and R7.
      Rules R1, R3 and R10 are deliberately overridden; the reasoning is kept
      in skills/interaction-standard/reference/provenance.md.

  evals/
      Rubric structure (weighted dimensions, blocking findings, baseline
      comparison) follows that project's approach.
